{
 "section_summary": "Two reports describe the July 1948 attempt to assassinate Japanese Communist Party leader Tokuda Kyuichi and the Soviet response. A Tokyo despatch then forwards a translation of Tokuda and Shiga Yoshio’s memoir, Eighteen Years in Prison. The excerpt covers Tokuda’s childhood, political development, the early Communist Party, arrests, imprisonment, and the party’s court strategy.",
